From 6c2d635aaa1f56403d22dc19529911a1d0948104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:26:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): resolve session-control owners from the project
 tree; re-read after an owner miss [daveey]

"Session controls unavailable: Session owner could not be resolved (session.control.read)"
stayed on a resumed day-old local chat (20261029_140918_f8947c, 10-30 15:57 PT). After the
restart its only loaded row was the sidebar project tree: the resume found the owner there
(cachedSessionRow reads the tree), but the sync owner ladder (ownerLookupSessionRows) never
looked at the tree, a local-primary bare-profile owner is not hinted, and primary events are
untagged, so the composer's read failed closed and was never retried.

- ownerLookupSessionRows includes project-tree rows (same owner stamps), memoized by input
  identity.
- An owner-resolution miss in refreshSessionControl arms a local re-check (owner-bearing
  atoms + 2 s poll, 15 min cap) that re-reads once the owner ladder resolves. Nothing is
  sent while unresolved: still fail-closed, no ambient fallback.
- Owner misses (read and action) and the later recovery log to desktop.log.
